<bx:output>
<div class="container py-5">
	<div class="c-project-hero">
		<p class="c-project-hero__eyebrow">Project</p>
		<h1 class="c-project-hero__title">boxlang-express-auth</h1>
		<p class="c-project-hero__tagline">Third-party sign-in for <a href="/projects/boxlang-express" class="c-post-link">boxlang-express</a> apps: a generic OAuth2 core, a generic <a href="https://openid.net/connect/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="c-post-link">OpenID Connect</a> provider, and presets for GitHub, Google, Microsoft, GitLab and Apple. Your app decides who a provider identity is; the module runs the flow, guards routes (WebSocket upgrades included), links extra accounts, and keeps the session honest.</p>
		<div class="c-project-hero__actions">
			<a href="/projects/boxlang-express-auth/docs/getting-started" class="btn btn-primary-custom">Read the Docs</a>
			<a href="https://github.com/robertz/boxlang-express-auth" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-outline-custom">View on GitHub</a>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="c-project-features">
		<div class="c-project-feature">
			<p class="c-project-feature__title"><i class="bi bi-people"></i> Six ways in</p>
			<p class="c-project-feature__body">GitHub, Google (with a Workspace domain limit), Microsoft Entra ID (with tenant control), GitLab, Apple, and any OIDC issuer such as Keycloak or Authelia.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="c-project-feature">
			<p class="c-project-feature__title"><i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i> The hard parts, done</p>
			<p class="c-project-feature__body">PKCE on every login, single-use expiring <code>state</code>, session regeneration, and ID tokens checked for signature, issuer, audience, expiry and nonce. Provider tokens are never stored.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="c-project-feature">
			<p class="c-project-feature__title"><i class="bi bi-link-45deg"></i> Linking and logout</p>
			<p class="c-project-feature__body">A signed-in user can attach another provider account, and signing out of an OIDC provider can continue at the issuer, so single sign-on ends where it started.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="c-project-feature">
			<p class="c-project-feature__title"><i class="bi bi-check2-square"></i> Testable</p>
			<p class="c-project-feature__body">A test provider signs users in through the real routes from your own specs, with no provider account and no network.</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="c-post__body c-docs-body">
		<div class="bx-callout"><strong>Running on this site</strong>"Sign in with Google" and "Sign in with GitHub" here run on boxlang-express-auth, for commenters and for the admin, where a passkey from <a href="/projects/bx-passkeys" class="c-post-link">bx-passkeys</a> is still required on top.</div>
	</div>

	<p class="c-post-sidebar__label mb-3 mt-4">Quick start</p>
	<div class="c-post__body c-docs-body">
<pre class="bx-code"><span class="bx-code-label">bash</span><code>install-bx-module boxlang-express,boxlang-express-auth --local</code></pre>
<pre class="bx-code"><span class="bx-code-label">javascript</span><code>auth = boxExpressAuth( {
	verify  : ( identity, tokens, req ) =&gt; users.findOrCreateFromIdentity( identity ),
	loadUser: ( id ) =&gt; users.get( id )
} )

auth.provider( "github", boxExpressAuthGitHub( {
	clientId    : getSystemSetting( "GITHUB_CLIENT_ID" ),
	clientSecret: getSystemSetting( "GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET" ),
	callbackUrl : "https://example.com/auth/github/callback"
} ) )

app.use( boxExpressSession( { resave: false, saveUninitialized: false } ) )
app.use( "/auth", auth.routes() )

app.get( "/dashboard", auth.required(), ( req, res ) =&gt; res.json( { user: req.user } ) )</code></pre>
	</div>
	<p class="mt-3"><a href="/projects/boxlang-express-auth/docs/getting-started" class="c-post-link">Routes, guards and what happens on the callback &rarr;</a></p>
</div>
</bx:output>
